            "text": "The legislative process differs in the U.S. House of Representatives and the Senate, with the House being larger and more diverse, and the Senate having more informal rules and unlimited debate.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "1",
            "text": "The House of Representatives has a Speaker of the House, while the Senate has a Majority Leader and a Minority Leader.",
